S3ADRAW V1.3 - README
---------------------

This file is for users of V1.2 who wish to upgrade to V1.3.  New users 
should use the file README.NEW, coupled with the full instructions.

To upgrade from V1.2, simply replace the old DRAWS3A2.APP file with the 
new DRAWS3A3.APP.  To make the setup more configurable, I have taken out 
the Help file as a separate overlay, and made it optional.  If you do 
want to use On-Line Help then put the DRAWS3AH.HLP file in an \APP\S3ADRAW\
Sub-Directory.

The first major change you will notice that is that I have cut the price of 
registration.  I'm afraid market forces have forced me into that, the 
program was not selling, and there are other, more powerful drawing programs 
around at a similar price.  I can sympathise with anyone who may feel they 
have been penalised by registering early, so I am prepared to offer a free 
registration to any of my other programs (except S3ABANK), as a form of
compensation.  Please let me know if you want to take advantage of this 
offer, details of the programs are in REGISTER.TXT.

As far as the program is concerned you will not notice much difference.  
What has happened is that my official BETA tester, Andy Waller, has been 
through the program with a fine toothcomb, and identified a large number of 
bugs, and made some good suggestions on how the program logic could be 
improved (For example, using the NEW FILE option from the System Screen
now takes you directly to the Editor rather than the Viewer).  These have 
all been incorporated.  

However, you will also see the following major changes:

a.    If you accidentally start a Zoom, Esc will now cancel it.	
b.    An optional Grid of lines or dots is now available in the Editor.
c.    When you Import a Picture, you now fine-tune the location before 
      finally accepting it.	
d.    The Info Window now shows the selected colour in Bold, in case you do 
      not have the Status Window in view.
e.    I have combined the Font and Style options into a single option.
f.    You can now use the extended character set (ASCII Code 128-254) in the
      text entry mode.  Just hold down the Control key and type in the code.
g.    I have added a new Tool in the Editor called 'Export Area', to allow 
      you to save part of the screen as a PIC file.

Hope you like the improvements.

If you get a chance, you can always visit my home page on the World-Wide Web, where
there are full details of all my programs, and news of any upgrades or enhancements.
The address is :  http://ourworld.compuserve.com/homepages/alanrichey

In the future, I intend to leave 'Beta' versions of the next versions of the 
programs on this site, as each new enhancement is incorporated.  If you don't mind 
taking the odd risk, that will be a way of continually updating your program.

Cheers

Al

